maximum has the unconditional exact below-threshold certificate

  5|4|1264381632596|188505,25402,1677710|415025,-353402,836862|38025,-6952,8313149|318873,-67684,994881

Independent verification command:

  python3 04-computation/imaginary_quadratic_class_rank_certificate_tool_20260824.py \
    verify --pari-gp /tmp/oct-class-tools-20260824/root/usr/bin/gp \
    '5|4|1264381632596|188505,25402,1677710|415025,-353402,836862|38025,-6952,8313149|318873,-67684,994881'

Verification output:

  PURE_PYTHON_VERIFY=PASS|ell=5|r=4|D=1264381632596|squarefree_core_factors=[(233, 1), (1283, 1), (1057391, 1)]|mitm_halves=25,25
  REDUCED_FORMS=188505,25402,1677710|415025,-353402,836862|38025,-6952,8313149|318873,-67684,994881
  PARI_AUDIT=PASS|h=680000|cyc=[1360, 10, 10, 5]|ell_rank=4|halves=25,25

The pure verifier proves the displayed subgroup lower bound without relying
on PARI's class-group invariant factors.  It does not prove that no row has
larger rank, and it does not claim the challenge pair (5,6).
